{"slug":"m-sh-y","ar":"م ش ي","total":23,"core":"walking","forms":[{"ar":"مَّشَ","kind":"verb","form":1,"count":21,"gloss":"To walk","word":"masha","ex":{"s":25,"a":63,"p":4,"ar":["وَعِبَادُ","ٱلرَّحْمَـٰنِ","ٱلَّذِينَ","يَمْشُونَ","عَلَى","ٱلْأَرْضِ","هَوْنًا","وَإِذَا","خَاطَبَهُمُ","ٱلْجَـٰهِلُونَ","قَالُوا۟","سَلَـٰمًا"],"en":"And the servants of the Most Merciful are those who walk upon the earth easily, and when the ignorant address them [harshly], they say [words of] peace"}},{"ar":"مَشْي","kind":"noun","form":null,"count":1,"gloss":"walk, gait","word":null,"ex":{"s":31,"a":19,"p":3,"ar":["وَٱقْصِدْ","فِى","مَشْيِكَ","وَٱغْضُضْ","مِن","صَوْتِكَ ۚ","إِنَّ","أَنكَرَ","ٱلْأَصْوَٰتِ","لَصَوْتُ","ٱلْحَمِيرِ"],"en":"And be moderate in your pace and lower your voice; indeed, the most disagreeable of sounds is the voice of donkeys"}},{"ar":"مَّشَّآء","kind":"adjective","form":null,"count":1,"gloss":"going about","word":null,"ex":{"s":68,"a":11,"p":2,"ar":["هَمَّازٍ","مَّشَّآءٍۭ","بِنَمِيمٍ"],"en":"[And] scorner, going about with malicious gossip"}}],"surahs":[[24,3],[25,3],[67,3],[17,2],[20,2],[31,2],[2,1],[6,1],[7,1],[28,1],[32,1],[38,1],[57,1],[68,1]]}